editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:199:1. **Seln and Shadow (coordinator ruling not applied).** The task's standing ruling says Seln learns why Shadow was sealed "in Book 6 Ch15, in this movement, as the plan and Book 5's ledger reserve it", and to follow the packet for how much. Every source I can find places that telling at **source** Book 6 Ch15, *The Cache*: BOOK_MAP §3 item 15 ("Cael tells Seln the mechanism; the Shadow seal and its cost; 'You kept my file too, then.'"), §6 (Seln "does not know a sealed thing exists until M6"), §9 (the integration mechanism "Expands to Seln only (M6)"), and B5's BOOK_MAP/packets ("B6 Ch15 tells him", meaning the source chapter). Edition chapter 15 is in M3, which may be the source of the confusion. The M3 packet calls for no telling at all ("Seln's method shown; his case not mentioned aloud"), and telling him why Shadow is sealed would require telling him the integration mechanism four movements early, and would strand the Tier A line "You kept my file too, then." So **Seln is not told in M3**. If the owner does want it here, it needs a packet line, and the cache scene in M6 will need replanning.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/plan-audit.md:7:There is one **M8 drafting caution, not an M7 defect**: the protected Tier B minute calls the declining party “the evaluator of record,” while the closed ledger calls Gault Halcenvane's evaluator of record and the M7 page sends the certification request to the Archmarshal. The protected words still govern M8. M8 must not use them to relabel Vastin as Halcenvane's evaluator of record; in the surrounding prose, Gault remains the house's evaluator and Vastin remains the Archmarshal/certifying office. If the coordinator does not accept “evaluator of record” as the minute's certification-role label, that protected line—not M7—needs an owner ruling before M8 is drafted.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/plan-audit.md:44:The binding shape is explicit in `BOOK_MAP.md:112`: “the ruling in the year's last month; the Line crossed after the year's close.” The last-month row says “Closing sittings; Ilsev; the ruling; the council; the last bout” (`BOOK_MAP.md:122`), followed by “Four days before the year's close → after the close” (`BOOK_MAP.md:123`). M8 enters in “The academic year's last month. Two closing sittings at Ostrand. Brom's review on the year's last Fifth-day” (`packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:13`). M9 enters “The morning after the last bout, four days before the academic year's close” (`packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:13`) and must end after the Line (`packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:36`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/plan-audit.md:62:**Governing text.** The coordinator says: “THE VELMERE LETTER (day 45) stays SEALED … it is BOOK_MAP §4e #10's unopened letter for M7” (`STATE_LEDGER.md:563`), carries it sealed through M5 (`STATE_LEDGER.md:808`) and M6 (`STATE_LEDGER.md:909,920`), and overrides the looser §4e wording about an arrival four weeks before the ruling. M8 assumes “The second Velmere envelope unopened” (`packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:13`) and further requires that Brom “does not open the envelope” (`packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:32`). M9 makes no contrary assumption.
