editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/plan-audit.stdout.log:5096:+There is one **M8 drafting caution, not an M7 defect**: the protected Tier B minute calls the declining party “the evaluator of record,” while the closed ledger calls Gault Halcenvane's evaluator of record and the M7 page sends the certification request to the Archmarshal. The protected words still govern M8. M8 must not use them to relabel Vastin as Halcenvane's evaluator of record; in the surrounding prose, Gault remains the house's evaluator and Vastin remains the Archmarshal/certifying office. If the coordinator does not accept “evaluator of record” as the minute's certification-role label, that protected line—not M7—needs an owner ruling before M8 is drafted.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/plan-audit.stdout.log:5132:+The binding shape is explicit in `BOOK_MAP.md:112`: “the ruling in the year's last month; the Line crossed after the year's close.” The last-month row says “Closing sittings; Ilsev; the ruling; the council; the last bout” (`BOOK_MAP.md:122`), followed by “Four days before the year's close → after the close” (`BOOK_MAP.md:123`). M8 enters in “The academic year's last month. Two closing sittings at Ostrand. Brom's review on the year's last Fifth-day” (`packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:13`). M9 enters “The morning after the last bout, four days before the academic year's close” (`packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:13`) and must end after the Line (`packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:36`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/plan-audit.stdout.log:5150:+**Governing text.** The coordinator says: “THE VELMERE LETTER (day 45) stays SEALED … it is BOOK_MAP §4e #10's unopened letter for M7” (`STATE_LEDGER.md:563`), carries it sealed through M5 (`STATE_LEDGER.md:808`) and M6 (`STATE_LEDGER.md:909,920`), and overrides the looser §4e wording about an arrival four weeks before the ruling. M8 assumes “The second Velmere envelope unopened” (`packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:13`) and further requires that Brom “does not open the envelope” (`packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:32`). M9 makes no contrary assumption.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/plan-audit.stdout.log:5158:+**Governing text.** The day-76 gate is fixed in the closed M4 ledger (`STATE_LEDGER.md:683,694,743`). The road attack remains unreported (`STATE_LEDGER.md:814,852`), while `BOOK_MAP.md:638` permits only the two already-completed faction moves and forbids a third. M8 requires “nobody dishonest anywhere” and keeps Jent counsel, not a faction face (`packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:17,34`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/plan-audit.stdout.log:5166:+**Governing text.** M7 calls for “the proceedings' request for certification renewed; he declines in one line; nothing else” (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:22`) and limits him to “one line of declination” as the operative act (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:38`). His POV limit forbids a report, file, alliance, departure, mechanism knowledge, or theory of the layer (`BOOK_MAP.md:491`). M8 protects the exact minute: “*Evaluation-protocol certification: declined by the evaluator of record; proceeding on the presiding seat's authority.*” (`BOOK_MAP.md:613–614`; `packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:29`). The ledger separately fixes “Magister Gault evaluator of record” (`BOOK_MAP.md:22`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:84`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/plan-audit.stdout.log:5168:+**Ruling.** M7 supplies every fact the protected M8 minute needs: a refusal, a withheld certificate, and statutory authority to proceed. It adds no forbidden act. M8 must quote its Tier B line verbatim, while its surrounding narration must preserve the distinct offices: Gault is Halcenvane's evaluator of record; Vastin is the Archmarshal who withholds certification. This is the audit's sole carry caution.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/plan-audit.stdout.log:5174:+**Governing text.** Havel may know “The Level 4 marker he was told to stand down about; the unplaceable seal; his own note,” but “Never connects the seal or the flag to falsification. The note stops at six entries” (`BOOK_MAP.md:493`). M7 requires “he rereads six entries; he does not write a seventh” (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:22,38`), and M8 owns “the transfer request; six entries, done” (`packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:22`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/plan-audit.stdout.log:5190:+**Governing text.** The plan expressly orders “Night spar, Cael and Lira, closed floor (she asks for the rate he never shows)” (`BOOK_MAP.md:352`) and says the private floor is where the circle is honest with its bodies (`BOOK_MAP.md:425–426`). M7 repeats: “the closed floor, no witnesses; she decides to say nothing” (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:24`). The restriction is only that “The band's ceiling is never exceeded in front of the school” (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:36`); M8 still owns the Norhold rates and beyond “shown on the bluff for the first time” publicly (`BOOK_MAP.md:288–293`; `packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:25`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/plan-audit.stdout.log:5198:+**Governing text.** M7 says, “The decision may be felt; it is not made” (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:33`) and assigns the night-road exercise to Brom's counting (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:25`). M8 owns the actual council choice: “five hands, Seln's last” (`BOOK_MAP.md:266–272,285–287`; `packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:24`). M9 then requires five to cross the Line while Ephram stays (`packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:31`).
