editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/plan-audit.stdout.log:6566:+**Governing text.** The day-76 gate is fixed in the closed M4 ledger (`STATE_LEDGER.md:683,694,743`). The road attack remains unreported (`STATE_LEDGER.md:814,852`), while `BOOK_MAP.md:638` permits only the two already-completed faction moves and forbids a third. M8 requires “nobody dishonest anywhere” and keeps Jent counsel, not a faction face (`packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:17,34`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/plan-audit.stdout.log:6574:+**Governing text.** M7 calls for “the proceedings' request for certification renewed; he declines in one line; nothing else” (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:22`) and limits him to “one line of declination” as the operative act (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:38`). His POV limit forbids a report, file, alliance, departure, mechanism knowledge, or theory of the layer (`BOOK_MAP.md:491`). M8 protects the exact minute: “*Evaluation-protocol certification: declined by the evaluator of record; proceeding on the presiding seat's authority.*” (`BOOK_MAP.md:613–614`; `packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:29`). The ledger separately fixes “Magister Gault evaluator of record” (`BOOK_MAP.md:22`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:84`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/plan-audit.stdout.log:6576:+**Ruling.** M7 supplies every fact the protected M8 minute needs: a refusal, a withheld certificate, and statutory authority to proceed. It adds no forbidden act. M8 must quote its Tier B line verbatim, while its surrounding narration must preserve the distinct offices: Gault is Halcenvane's evaluator of record; Vastin is the Archmarshal who withholds certification. This is the audit's sole carry caution.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/plan-audit.stdout.log:6582:+**Governing text.** Havel may know “The Level 4 marker he was told to stand down about; the unplaceable seal; his own note,” but “Never connects the seal or the flag to falsification. The note stops at six entries” (`BOOK_MAP.md:493`). M7 requires “he rereads six entries; he does not write a seventh” (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:22,38`), and M8 owns “the transfer request; six entries, done” (`packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:22`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/plan-audit.stdout.log:6598:+**Governing text.** The plan expressly orders “Night spar, Cael and Lira, closed floor (she asks for the rate he never shows)” (`BOOK_MAP.md:352`) and says the private floor is where the circle is honest with its bodies (`BOOK_MAP.md:425–426`). M7 repeats: “the closed floor, no witnesses; she decides to say nothing” (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:24`). The restriction is only that “The band's ceiling is never exceeded in front of the school” (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:36`); M8 still owns the Norhold rates and beyond “shown on the bluff for the first time” publicly (`BOOK_MAP.md:288–293`; `packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:25`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/plan-audit.stdout.log:6606:+**Governing text.** M7 says, “The decision may be felt; it is not made” (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:33`) and assigns the night-road exercise to Brom's counting (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:25`). M8 owns the actual council choice: “five hands, Seln's last” (`BOOK_MAP.md:266–272,285–287`; `packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:24`). M9 then requires five to cross the Line while Ephram stays (`packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:31`).
