editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7602:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:23:- **The Copper final (developed; the series' best-matched bout since Cael–Brom).** Two clocks: Brom's hardening fades past about four minutes, and Lira has three bursts with the fourth "the one she told him about." **1:** she asks the seam three ways and the counter is *already there*; it isn't speed but a different skeleton. She grins. **2:** Brom takes it; Rooke taught him to *stop finishing the absorption*, eating a fifth of every strike; two bursts; she is put on the boards. **3 (four minutes eleven):** the least Lira-shaped thing she has ever done — walking backward around the floor twice on foot, *spending his clock*; the stretch to five beats; the third burst; heel behind the knee. **4 (eleven seconds):** he goes straight at the hip, no disguise. The fourth burst. She lands on the bad hip *on purpose* so the fold carries her during a beat that can't move. "She used a wound as a mechanism." He hauls her up; neither lets go for three seconds.
