editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7683:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:295:- ch52, exchange 4: "The third exchange had held him on the iron for four minutes and eleven seconds, and the turn of the glass had not given that back; eleven seconds into the fourth…"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7694:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/compiled-prompt.md:491:It came the way the first one had come, thirty-seven nights ago, on this cot. There was no sound and no light and no direction it came from; there was the quiet first, the quiet before a thought arrives whole, and then the turning over, and then, in the dark place behind his breastbone where nothing had lit since the word, something written.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7695:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/compiled-prompt.md:553:He closed the book and set it on the shelf beside Hesk's leather one. He lay down very carefully on his back, which was the only way left that did not hurt, and found that it hurt anyway. He lay looking at the beam with its old nail holes in the light of Yeni's lamp, and felt the two things sitting quietly side by side in the dark behind his breastbone, the one that leaned and the one that pressed, and listened to the wheezing man begin to whistle.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7696:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/compiled-prompt.md:667:He thought about two lines of figures in the dark behind his breastbone where there had been one. There were two doors, perhaps, where he had thought there was only one, and he did not know where either of them went, or which of them he had come through, or whether there were others in the dark he had not found yet. He did not know what Kestrel had been, or what Feryn's hand had been, or whether Lira's three months and Feryn's one second were the same thing at all.
