editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7726:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-cold-prompt.md:551:By Cael's private count the exchange had run four minutes and eleven seconds. He stayed sitting and watched Lira walk back to her chalk.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7727:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-cold-prompt.md:567:The fourth exchange lasted eleven seconds.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7728:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-cold-prompt.md:591:The first belonged to Brom: four minutes of iron and eleven seconds more had put his turn on the fifth count instead of the fourth, a hair late.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7729:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-cold-prompt.md:1341:Cael had looked at it every time he came into this room and had never once got a name for it. Squat, copper, three short legs, a little larger than two fists: that was the pot. Out of its lid stood a glass straw scored with lines as close as a comb's teeth. A small brass plate on its belly carried a date of calibration in paint, and the date was this month's. The clerk set it on its legs on the oak a pace from the crossing and stepped back.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7761:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-cold.md:39:- "four minutes of iron and eleven seconds more had put his turn on the fifth count" (Chapter 52, exchange four) uses the length of exchange three (4:11 by Cael's count) as if it were Brom's whole clock, though Chapter 51 says both clocks "started the moment the two of them walked out" and exchange one ran "most of two minutes". Either the clock is cumulative hard contact, in which case the number is wrong, or it restarted, in which case the earlier sentence is. A listener who has been doing the sums, as the chapter invites, will stop.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7762:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-cold.md:44:Observation to keep: the whole exchange-four sequence (eleven seconds, four reasons it was not the end) is the clearest piece of fight-writing in the movement and should not be touched.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7763:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-cold.md:65:- Gault, after trial four: "This wing measures six things. Five of them have moved and one hasn't." At that moment four trials have run; the cold runs have not. The sentence is true by the end of the sitting (board, read, combined, cold board, cold read moved; plate did not) but it is said before the instruments have said it, which is precisely the thing Gault would not do.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7764:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-cold.md:102:| Action / suspense | 8 | Ch 52 "The fourth exchange lasted eleven seconds"; Ch 55 the four pieces | Trackable contest with named costs; earned length. Docked for the cumulative-clock wobble | High |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7765:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-cold.md:115:- **Brom's clock.** Ch 51: both clocks "started the moment the two of them walked out"; Ch 51 end of exchange one: "His four minutes had begun"; Ch 52: "four minutes of iron and eleven seconds more" taken from exchange three alone. Three different start points for one clock.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7766:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-cold.md:145:- **Observed issue:** *eleven* carries roughly nineteen unrelated counts across six chapters. "Four minutes of iron and eleven seconds more" treats exchange three's duration as Brom's whole clock after Chapter 51 said both clocks started at the walk-out. The glance tally names six people and claims seven. The ledger says "Drifts: two" and "it never flickered" in one entry. Brom's strapped hand appears without a cause.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7785:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/REPAIR-BRIEF.md:72:   started" and ch52's "four minutes of iron and eleven seconds more" agree.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7800:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:135:He had copied the three lines letter by letter from the back of the Log, and checked them twice against the page, and then once more against the place in the dark behind his breastbone where they had been written first.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7801:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:349:The category was not for anybody whose classification could not be read. It was for people who did not have one. Section four gave an assessor the power to put a practitioner into the category, and section one, three pages earlier, said who could be in it. A boy whose Arbiter had returned nothing would be in it. A boy whose return had been lost, or never recorded, would be in it. And a boy whose Arbiter had taken eleven seconds and then returned a word, a real word, a word with four instances and a statute of its own in the Supplementary Register, and a brass plate that had lit eleven seconds late, had a primary classification. He had more of one than anybody in the district. It simply was not one the standard framework could use.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7802:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:359:*Three. Section one also says what a primary classification is: what the Arbiter returned, entered in the registry, including the Supplementary Register. Mine was entered there. Statute nineteen. Four instances. It resolved; the plate lit.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7803:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:475:"Section one also says what a primary classification is. *The classification returned by the practitioner's Arbiter at Kindling and entered in the registry, including any entry made in the Supplementary Register.*" He did not hurry. "Mine was returned at Kindling. It took eleven seconds. It's entered in the Supplementary Register, statute nineteen, with an incidence count. I have a primary classification. It isn't one the standard framework can use, which is why section four's first half fits me. But section four lets you enter a practitioner into the category, and section one says who the category is for. It's for practitioners without one. Not being assessable by ordinary means isn't the same as not being classified."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7804:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:1631:He knew the way now, a little. He went into the dark place behind his breastbone and found the Wind there first, the leaning thing, the readiness, the shape the step had left. He went past it, carefully. Beyond it there was the other one, which he had felt sitting beside the first since the night after Feryn and had not touched. It did not lean. It was heavier than that, and lower, and quieter: a sort of weight in the dark that seemed to be waiting to be picked up, as a sack waits on a quay.
