editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7816:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:3017:**Fragments & progression.** None. Arbiter not consulted (dark since the word; no attempt staged — the courtyard is M3's). Circuit: **unrated, 0–1** (loss to Renn, Cu3 Blade, fourth exchange, by the flat, called). A return bout with Renn is requested at a month, "inclined to give it". **Instance count:** none logged. The Renn third exchange is filed "whole and unexamined", and the cart sits beside it uncounted ("he did not let himself count them, because counting them would have been the first step toward a word"). M3's sparring plant can be "first instance" as planned.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7817:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:3098:- No fragments, no notices. The Arbiter is **dark**: absence, tested at length on the night of day 28.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7818:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:3834:At age 14, every person undergoes Kindling: the moment their latent Path potential activates. Kindling is involuntary — it happens regardless of whether the person is ready. An **Arbiter** appears at the moment of Kindling: a small glowing sigil that only the Kindling person can see and hear. The Arbiter evaluates the person's internal architecture and assigns their Path classification.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7819:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:3856:As a practitioner advances through ranks, new abilities manifest — presented by the Arbiter as visible ability declarations, experienced as text-like constructs in the practitioner's perception. These are called **Path declarations** and are specific to the practitioner's Path type.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7820:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:3964:- **The line is sharp, not a gradient:** a stride inside, the Arbiter is dark and no declaration renders; a stride outside, it is back — practitioners describe the return as a clock resuming (Lira's clock). Every Arbiter in a party fails identically, at the same stride, one way and back the same, regardless of Path or tier (B7 Ch10–11, Ch18, Ch21).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7834:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/review-cold-prompt.md:135:He had copied the three lines letter by letter from the back of the Log, and checked them twice against the page, and then once more against the place in the dark behind his breastbone where they had been written first.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7835:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/review-cold-prompt.md:349:The category was not for anybody whose classification could not be read. It was for people who did not have one. Section four gave an assessor the power to put a practitioner into the category, and section one, three pages earlier, said who could be in it. A boy whose Arbiter had returned nothing would be in it. A boy whose return had been lost, or never recorded, would be in it. And a boy whose Arbiter had taken eleven seconds and then returned a word, a real word, a word with four instances and a statute of its own in the Supplementary Register, and a brass plate that had lit eleven seconds late, had a primary classification. He had more of one than anybody in the district. It simply was not one the standard framework could use.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7836:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/review-cold-prompt.md:359:*Three. Section one also says what a primary classification is: what the Arbiter returned, entered in the registry, including the Supplementary Register. Mine was entered there. Statute nineteen. Four instances. It resolved; the plate lit.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7837:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/review-cold-prompt.md:475:"Section one also says what a primary classification is. *The classification returned by the practitioner's Arbiter at Kindling and entered in the registry, including any entry made in the Supplementary Register.*" He did not hurry. "Mine was returned at Kindling. It took eleven seconds. It's entered in the Supplementary Register, statute nineteen, with an incidence count. I have a primary classification. It isn't one the standard framework can use, which is why section four's first half fits me. But section four lets you enter a practitioner into the category, and section one says who the category is for. It's for practitioners without one. Not being assessable by ordinary means isn't the same as not being classified."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7838:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/review-cold-prompt.md:1631:He knew the way now, a little. He went into the dark place behind his breastbone and found the Wind there first, the leaning thing, the readiness, the shape the step had left. He went past it, carefully. Beyond it there was the other one, which he had felt sitting beside the first since the night after Feryn and had not touched. It did not lean. It was heavier than that, and lower, and quieter: a sort of weight in the dark that seemed to be waiting to be picked up, as a sack waits on a quay.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7839:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/pre-repair/chapter-49.md:101:"Section one also says what a primary classification is. *The classification returned by the practitioner's Arbiter at Kindling and entered in the registry, including any entry made in the Supplementary Register.*" He did not hurry. "Mine was returned at Kindling. It took eleven seconds. It's entered in the Supplementary Register, statute nineteen, with an incidence count. I have a primary classification. It isn't one the standard framework can use, which is why section four's first half fits me. But section four lets you enter a practitioner into the category, and section one says who the category is for. It's for practitioners without one. Not being assessable by ordinary means isn't the same as not being classified."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7842:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/review-cold.md:11:**Orientation, arriving at chapter 48 mid-book.** I was oriented within two pages. The chalked post with its three columns told me the mechanics at once: a boy (Cael, fourteen, though the number does not appear until ch51) has a "step" he can ask for, it costs him, and Lira makes him account for the cost. I picked up the rest by use rather than explanation: the Cinder House and Vell's book, Torvin's lodging house, Hesk in Denvash, the Compact's post at the top of the fish steps, Coss, an objection filed in the autumn, a "second notice" that arrived inside him after the Feryn loss. Terms I never fully understood but never needed to: Kindling, Arbiter, instance, statute nineteen, Fourthweek, "the plate lit eleven seconds late." The one word that cost me real friction is "the post," which means Lira's chalked post in the yard and also the Compact building at the head of the fish steps; the sentence "Not the post, either; it's Vell's" (113) and then "at the post, Ardenmere" (193) made me stop and re-sort. By ch49 it was clear. The opening sentence, "Properly, it turned out, meant a column," is an in-joke on a prior line I have not read; it reads as a wink I was not party to.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7843:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/pre-repair/chapter-48.md:71:He had copied the three lines letter by letter from the back of the Log, and checked them twice against the page, and then once more against the place in the dark behind his breastbone where they had been written first.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7844:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/pre-repair/chapter-48.md:285:The category was not for anybody whose classification could not be read. It was for people who did not have one. Section four gave an assessor the power to put a practitioner into the category, and section one, three pages earlier, said who could be in it. A boy whose Arbiter had returned nothing would be in it. A boy whose return had been lost, or never recorded, would be in it. And a boy whose Arbiter had taken eleven seconds and then returned a word, a real word, a word with four instances and a statute of its own in the Supplementary Register, and a brass plate that had lit eleven seconds late, had a primary classification. He had more of one than anybody in the district. It simply was not one the standard framework could use.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7845:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/pre-repair/chapter-48.md:295:*Three. Section one also says what a primary classification is: what the Arbiter returned, entered in the registry, including the Supplementary Register. Mine was entered there. Statute nineteen. Four instances. It resolved; the plate lit.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7850:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/pre-repair/chapter-52.md:345:He knew the way now, a little. He went into the dark place behind his breastbone and found the Wind there first, the leaning thing, the readiness, the shape the step had left. He went past it, carefully. Beyond it there was the other one, which he had felt sitting beside the first since the night after Feryn and had not touched. It did not lean. It was heavier than that, and lower, and quieter: a sort of weight in the dark that seemed to be waiting to be picked up, as a sack waits on a quay.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7866:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-008/compiled-prompt.md:621:Nobody ever had. In a year of wardens and evaluators and brass plates and panels, everybody who looked at him had been looking for a line to fill in or a figure to post. Nothing in her face was going to be written down anywhere. She had come across something that was on none of her tables, and in front of eight thousand people she had stopped to find out what it was.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7867:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-008/compiled-prompt.md:1383:| Cael | Sixteen (turned on the eleventh of Sowing, Book 4; the date is never set beside a season word, OWNER #35). Healthy, rested, and trained: sixty-one floor sessions over the recess. No current injuries: B4 closed him fit (the quarter-burst's hip load ended the night of the twenty-third of Reaping; the plate's right-shoulder ache eased by the week's end). The leading hip carries the Wind fragment's old strain (crest to inner knee after a hard evening), and the landing beat is still unshortened. The right shoulder pays Pressure, "four blows a sitting", the circle's private cap and not a registry schedule (B4 ch62; OWNER #36: the plate/Pressure shoulder is the right). The Shadow fragment's rent runs from waking, spent or not; drifts come in the gaps, never in the work, and the weekly count is falling; the working ledger's day count since the stair and the protocol *Hold. First.* are the discipline. Arbiter dark since the Kindling. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7868:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-008/compiled-prompt.md:1426:- **Functional level:** Iron-equivalent in every evaluation. The registry sees [SHATTERED], unclassified, with the Suppression-Advisory Watch Level 4 (origin: registry sub-layer; authorizing office untraceable).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7869:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-008/compiled-prompt.md:2479:- Brom: the continental Copper plaque (dark wood, a brass plate, the bar-and-ring); the registry notice; the Velmere letter at the bottom of his kit.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7870:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-008/compiled-prompt.md:2541:- **The plaque:** dark wood, a brass plate, the bar-and-ring cut at the top, a line of small type.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7871:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-008/compiled-prompt.md:2734:  - the public house's brass plate in superseded registry wording;
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7872:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:551:By Cael's private count the exchange had run four minutes and eleven seconds. He stayed sitting and watched Lira walk back to her chalk.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7873:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:567:The fourth exchange lasted eleven seconds.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7874:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:591:The first belonged to Brom: four minutes of iron and eleven seconds more had put his turn on the fifth count instead of the fourth, a hair late.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7875:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:1341:Cael had looked at it every time he came into this room and had never once got a name for it. Squat, copper, three short legs, a little larger than two fists: that was the pot. Out of its lid stood a glass straw scored with lines as close as a comb's teeth. A small brass plate on its belly carried a date of calibration in paint, and the date was this month's. The clerk set it on its legs on the oak a pace from the crossing and stepped back.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7876:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:2777:| Suppression-Advisory Watch, Level 4, on the file | Havel (private note, three entries); Ilsev (filed a referral at the hearing); Coss (escalated, unanswered) | Its origin: nobody (LOCKED until B6) |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7877:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:2978:- Lira vs Nyle: eleven seconds, three touches, EXACTLY FOUR Wind bursts (the third exchange opens on a half-step with no Wind); the fifth-burst billing rule stands.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7878:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:3654:At age 14, every person undergoes Kindling: the moment their latent Path potential activates. Kindling is involuntary — it happens regardless of whether the person is ready. An **Arbiter** appears at the moment of Kindling: a small glowing sigil that only the Kindling person can see and hear. The Arbiter evaluates the person's internal architecture and assigns their Path classification.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7879:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:3676:As a practitioner advances through ranks, new abilities manifest — presented by the Arbiter as visible ability declarations, experienced as text-like constructs in the practitioner's perception. These are called **Path declarations** and are specific to the practitioner's Path type.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7880:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:3784:- **The line is sharp, not a gradient:** a stride inside, the Arbiter is dark and no declaration renders; a stride outside, it is back — practitioners describe the return as a clock resuming (Lira's clock). Every Arbiter in a party fails identically, at the same stride, one way and back the same, regardless of Path or tier (B7 Ch10–11, Ch18, Ch21).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7881:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:3916:- **The Copper final (developed; the series' best-matched bout since Cael–Brom).** Two clocks: Brom's hardening fades past about four minutes, and Lira has three bursts with the fourth "the one she told him about." **1:** she asks the seam three ways and the counter is *already there*; it isn't speed but a different skeleton. She grins. **2:** Brom takes it; Rooke taught him to *stop finishing the absorption*, eating a fifth of every strike; two bursts; she is put on the boards. **3 (four minutes eleven):** the least Lira-shaped thing she has ever done — walking backward around the floor twice on foot, *spending his clock*; the stretch to five beats; the third burst; heel behind the knee. **4 (eleven seconds):** he goes straight at the hip, no disguise. The fourth burst. She lands on the bad hip *on purpose* so the fold carries her during a beat that can't move. "She used a wound as a mechanism." He hauls her up; neither lets go for three seconds.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7914:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-008/recheck-r1.md:105:- *Her knowledge:* she knows her own assessed ceiling and the facilities office's margin from the brass plate on every sill ("the rating was always her own assessed ceiling and a margin", ch49), she has read the protocol ("You read everything", the head; her finger "ahead of his voice" down Umber's list, ch50), and the risk officer's terms are hers to repeat ("Masts at your ceiling. The barrier up. The rows back. A floor rated for you, on a frame", ch49). Nothing she says exceeds that.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7957:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:190:  - quarters with a sealed rated pane (brass plate);
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7964:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/pre-repair/chapter-52.md:105:By Cael's private count the exchange had run four minutes and eleven seconds. He stayed sitting and watched Lira walk back to her chalk.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7965:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/pre-repair/chapter-52.md:121:The fourth exchange lasted eleven seconds.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7966:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/pre-repair/chapter-52.md:145:The first belonged to Brom: four minutes of iron and eleven seconds more had put his turn on the fifth count instead of the fourth, a hair late.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7987:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-008/review-cold-prompt.md:575:It never did, anywhere. Every room she had slept in since she was sixteen had a single pane of thick glass set in lead, with a small brass plate on the sill to say what it was rated for, and the rating was always her own assessed ceiling and a margin. The program's facilities office ordered them. She had stopped trying latches years ago.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:7999:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/pre-repair/chapter-54.md:185:Cael had looked at it every time he came into this room and had never once got a name for it. Squat, copper, three short legs, a little larger than two fists: that was the pot. Out of its lid stood a glass straw scored with lines as close as a comb's teeth. A small brass plate on its belly carried a date of calibration in paint, and the date was this month's. The clerk set it on its legs on the oak a pace from the crossing and stepped back.
