editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:8018:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-008/review-editorial.md:155:Rhagen's semifinal line; the commercial last leaf (a copper; three paragraphs of "analysis"); the steward (narrow, tidy, keys on a cord, outer staff); the eastern Silver Five; the fishwife; the convening room (third floor; framed plans of every demonstration ring); the rider's shape; the new ring (§3, flag 7, with the figures); four healers; Daeva's rated pane with its brass plate, the marbled notebook, the garden court (pear tree; a red-spined history of the coastal leagues; the instructor's account with "composure" underlined twice), the coastal exhibition at fifteen, the design session in a hired warehouse among the coopers' yards (the report's "dry-goods" is not on the page), the pressure hour, the crooked lane, her lead instructor, delegation head, risk officer, a newer staffer and counsel's junior, all unnamed; "Gold at seventeen, which nobody had been before" and "The registry kept its living Storm practitioners on a single page"; the coastal fatality; Zerin known to Daeva since twelve; Vastin's four sorts of silence, the district office "with a leaking roof and no clerk", the emptied week, the struck advisory re-read, "This time he would stay"; the hill's figures; Rhagen's Wind; Marek's page; the standings reading's form (lowest first; the validation officer initialling; the inland house with no line; the furled Standard under a guard of two); the keeper's six sittings and cold room; the lock-keeper's forty-verse song and brass bell; Gault's ribbon; the powder wharf's two older masts; Karis's ruled column on Hesk's clock; "Then I'll stamp."; the honesty sheet; the pipe and the river; the card's wording; Seln's grey offcuts and sealing-wax knife; the ash already broken.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:8019:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-008/review-editorial.md:254:**Assessment.** The words are the edition's, the entry points are often new (the steward, the fishwife, the warehouse, the pressure hour, the garden bench, the brass plate, the sorts of silence, the pea in the pipe), and the invented scenes are clean. But in the fifteen scenes above the author drafted from the source's beat order rather than from an event list, which is what EDITION_BRIEF's 2026-10-02 note forbids and what the author's own report half-admits ("the tracking was in the scenes I remembered as scenes"). This is about three times M7's seventeen sentences. It does not sink the movement, because the gate's measurable test (8-word runs) is clean and the probe's close band is 14% rather than B3 M6's 23–32%; it is the reason the verdict carries a repair rather than a close.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths.stdout.log:8150:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:575:It never did, anywhere. Every room she had slept in since she was sixteen had a single pane of thick glass set in lead, with a small brass plate on the sill to say what it was rated for, and the rating was always her own assessed ceiling and a margin. The program's facilities office ordered them. She had stopped trying latches years ago.
