editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-001/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:20:| 5 | Served | 4,486 | 5 | **Day 8, First-day, second bell:** three riders at a walk on the last switchback, a case strapped across the saddle; Bracken's window empty because he has already seen them; the lodge-man stands; through the gate unmounted. **The records hall:** a registry officer in plain grey; Withrow at her ordinary pace, chosen; the protocol card; **joint service** (*Acknowledgment of Joint Service*, two signatures); the Compact's seal; she reads standing, in her old registry voice, **the first page** (Tier B; one phrase recomposed for the calendar). **"Given under the Compact's hand." / "I have signed that line myself. Nine hundred times."** Copies tonight; "Go up and tell Karis." **The reading room:** "Standard Arbiter protocol… exactly those?" (station, frame, declaration taught); "They read the hearing… every page we won on"; the assistant sent for the code, the transcript and the four rulings. **The bluff learns:** Lira pulled off the floor ("Records hall. Now."); Brom's bread; **the green form**, stamped by the wing, books the records hall for the night in Karis's name ("Somebody has been expecting us"); Ephram and the cohort; the board: *Halcenvane Academy has been served, and will answer within the time allowed.* **Evening at the window:** *They filed… Note the date. The season's open.* Withrow's voice "that would not shake" |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-001/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:22:| 7 | Corridor | 5,438 | 5 | **Paragraph nine:** Bracken knows *evaluation integrity* from his own filing (an Ostrand frame reading Stones a rank high); the counsel's twelve sections, never before turned on a person; "I'm the frame." / "A frame that will not read true comes off the floor." Remedy, paragraph 34. The counsel: "A count is evidence. Indignation never was." **Chapter fourteen** in Bracken's flattest voice (Tier B); "Somebody… imagined you." **Withrow's morning after**: the ferry pass, the guild hall, the sealed file, the house's letter; **"It's expulsion that follows you."**; the two restrictions and the daughter at her counter every week for a year. **Bracken's pocket calendar:** dated the first day, served the eighth, seven days at a walk ("sent to be watched getting here"), **due the twenty-second**; *respondent made default*. **Karis's six slips**; **"It's not a question. It's a corridor. Every door in it is real law, and every door opens one way."**; "The house will answer"; *fled*; four days. **The stratum note, sideways:** "They're trying to move him back inside the instrument." / "I don't know why that distinction feels important. Noting it." A question mark in Cael's notebook. **The residence awake for her:** Seln's lamp in the wing; Brom's tea kept hot for hours, four cups; Karis counts the room; "Thank you for the tea." Cael tells it; **Brom: "Corridor."**; **Lira: "What if the people didn't fail this time?"**; "Then there's a place where they read it wrong." **The first pole**, verbatim, in one pass; the records hall's lamps out in pairs; the copy on the sill, first page up, **waiting for better light** |
