editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-008/AUTHORSHIP.md:23:**Method.** `EVENT-LIST.md` was written first, in my own words, with the binding calendar and every scene's mechanics invented inside canon (the count of the room; both closings' rhetoric; the east hall rehearsal; the call days and the guesting-house; the wool press; the supplemental; the district station; the evaluation seat's return; Havel's copyist and his form; Brom's panel reported; the ruling's five heads; Seln's reading of the engrossment; the copy-sets; the council's order; the guidance note; Karis's bibliography; Withrow's arithmetic; the priced leaf; Lira's window; the board; all four exchanges; the boards custom). Drafting followed the list. The first full draft measured sentence mean 12.2 with 1.3% of sentences at forty words or more (clipped narration). I repaired it by reading: chapters 49, 51, 52, 53 and 54 were re-composed whole by hand, joining clipped statements that were one thought and keeping speech and the fight's counted beats short; chapters 48 and 50 were left as drafted. No script split or joined sentences. The only scripted edits were lists of exact old/new strings that I wrote by hand for small continuity fixes, each asserted to match exactly once.
