    34	
    35	The counsel was speaking. Cael could not hear a word. He saw her lay one finger on a line in the code and then on the sheet, and then on the code again, lower down, as a person does who is adding days. He saw the rule turn its quarter turn at the end of it.
    36	
    37	Withrow said something short, and the counsel answered, and then for a long moment nobody in that room spoke at all.
    38	
    39	Then Withrow reached across the table and shut the code herself, with one hand, quite gently. She drew the single sheet toward her and folded it once and put it inside her coat. She looked up as she did it, and saw him through the pane.
